  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe current solution uses a combination of greedy binary initialization, coordinate descent, and SLSQP smoothing to minimize the overlap integral. Our goal is to improve upon this by:\n1. Using level-set methods to more accurately solve the underlying continuous optimization problem\n2. Incorporating regularization to escape local minima\n3. Employing multi-resolution analysis to uncover better solutions at different scales\n4. Using more numerically stable optimization techniques\nThe key bottleneck is the non-convexity of the problem and the potential for local minima to trap the optimization process. We address this by combining regularization, multiple scales, and optimized initialization.\n\nMathematicalspecification:\n**Variables:**\n- h: Piecewise constant function at breakpoints {x1, x2, ..., xk} with values in [0,1]\n- \u03a3wi = 1 (integral constraint)\n\n**Objective:**\nminimize max_{t\u2208[-2,2]} \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+t)) dx\nWhere the integral is over the support [x_i, x_{i+1}].\n\n**Constraints:**\n0 \u2264 h_m(x) (binary case) \u2264 1\n\u2211 h(x_m) * dx = 1\n\n**Algorithm:**\n1. Define candidate function class  \n2. Formulate regularized objective: min_{h} max_t corr(h,1-h) + \u03bb\u2225h\u2225_{TV}\n3. Use projected gradient with coordinate descent\n4. Regularize to control flat regions\n\nImplementationprocedure:\n1. Parent validation:\n- Verify initial h satisfies \u2211h*dx=1\n- Clip to [0,1] and adjust sum\n2. Initialization:\n- Use step function at uniform points\n3. Optimization:\na. Perform coordinate-descent with gradient projection\nb. Regularize with TV-based penalty\nc. Use line searches to ensure convergence\n4. Candidate handler:\n- Monitor and accept better candidates\n- Retrain on improved solutions\n5. Multi-resolution escape:\n- Investigate coarser/finer grid representations\n- Use interpolation/decimation\n\nSearchchoicesandvariations:\n1. Alpha grid: 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10, 100 for regularization\n2. Resolution changes: 200, 400, 800 grid points\n3. Projection trust factors: \u03bb = [0.1, 0.25, 0.5]\n\nComputebudgetandrobustness:\n1. Master timing: 1100s total\n2. Check each major phase: coord_desc: 30%, optim_round: 50%, resolution: 20%\n3. Use memprofile to limit n_points < 800\n4. Prepare fallback if invalid solution detected\n\nValidationandreturncontract:\n1. Verify 0\u2264h\u22641 and sum(h)*dx=1\n2. Compute objective with np.correlate\n3. Ensure n_points is integer at least 200\nIf invalid solution, return parent representation.",
